@extends('layouts/buddy')
@section('title', 'Start with their fit')
<script client>
import { planningSize } from '~/app/Storefront/Catalog'
const weight = state('')
const height = state('')
const unit = state('imperial')
const result = state('')
const sizeCode = state('')
function checkSize(): void {
  const kg = unit() === 'metric'
  const suggestion = planningSize(Number(weight()) * (kg ? 2.2046226218 : 1), Number(height()) / (kg ? 2.54 : 1))
  result.set(suggestion.message)
  sizeCode.set(suggestion.code || '')
}
function clearResult(): void {
  result.set('')
  sizeCode.set('')
}
</script>
@section('content')
  <section class="section-space shell">
    <div class="max-w-2xl"><h1 class="section-title">Start with their shape.</h1><p class="mt-5 muted">A good fit begins with a few measurements and a little guidance. Find a wheelchair starting size, or measure up for a Rover cabin.</p></div>
    <div class="mt-8 notice">If loss of hind-leg use is new or sudden, seek urgent veterinary assessment. Do not delay treatment to measure or build a chair.</div>
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 mt-10">
      <div class="soft-panel">
        <h2 class="font-medium text-2xl">Find a starting size</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm muted">Start with weight and rear-leg height. The result helps narrow your choice; a complete fitting checks the rest. Measurements stay in your browser.</p>
        <form class="mt-7 space-y-5" @submit.prevent="checkSize()">
          <div class="field"><label for="units">Measurement units</label><select id="units" x-model="unit" @change="clearResult()"><option value="imperial">Pounds &amp; inches</option><option value="metric">Kilograms &amp; centimeters</option></select></div>
          <div class="grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2"><div class="field"><label for="weight">Weight ({{ unit() === 'metric' ? 'kg' : 'lb' }})</label><input id="weight" type="number" min="0.1" step="any" required x-model="weight" @input="clearResult()"></div><div class="field"><label for="height">Rear-leg height ({{ unit() === 'metric' ? 'cm' : 'in' }})</label><input id="height" type="number" min="0.1" step="any" required x-model="height" @input="clearResult()"></div></div>
          <Button type="submit" variant="bare" class="button-primary">Find their starting size</Button>
        </form>
        <div aria-live="polite" role="status" class="mt-6"><p data-fit-result>{{ result() }}</p><a :if="sizeCode()" :href="'/shop?size=' + sizeCode()" class="inline-flex mt-4 button-text">Explore this size</a></div>
      </div>
      <div><h2 class="font-medium text-2xl">The rest of the fit.</h2><div class="mt-6 feature-rule"><h3 class="font-semibold">Let a professional guide their posture.</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm muted">Ask your vet how to support your dog for measurements. Do not force standing or straighten a painful limb.</p></div><div class="feature-rule"><h3 class="font-semibold">Measure length and width, too.</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm muted">Body shape, harness position and wheel clearance matter alongside height and weight. Have the full set ready before confirming a fit.</p></div><div class="feature-rule"><h3 class="font-semibold">Choose the right kind of support.</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm muted">A rear-support chair depends on suitable front-leg strength and an appropriate care plan. Your professional can assess what your dog needs.</p></div><a href="/care" class="inline-flex mt-4 button-text">Care for every outing</a></div>
    </div>
    <section id="rover" class="mt-12 soft-panel"><h2 class="font-medium text-2xl">Room to ride in Buddy Rover.</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl muted">Measure seated height, lying length and shoulder width in a comfortable position. Allow room to settle, turn and change position. Ask your care professional about positioning if your dog needs support.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-sm muted">The final cabin dimensions and load limits will be published before Rover ordering opens. The wheelchair size result above does not select a Rover cabin.</p><a href="/rover" class="inline-flex mt-6 button-text">Explore Buddy Rover</a></section>
  </section>
@endsection
